343 - I Will Sing of My Redeemer
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 343
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[G]I will sing of my Redeemer, And [F#dim]His wondrous [D/F#]love [F#dim]to me;
[Am]On the cruel [F#dim]cross He [G]suffered, From the curse to set me free.
[F#dim]Sing, oh [D/F#]sing, of [Bm]my Redeemer, [Am]With His [Em/B]blood, He purchased [G]me.
[C/G]On the cross, He [G]sealed my pardon, [D7/C]Paid the debt, and made [Am]me free.

Refrain:
[G]Sing, oh sing, of [C/G]my Redeemer,
[G]With His blood, He purchased me.
[G/D]On the [D7]cross, He sealed [Bm]my pardon,
[G]Paid the debt, and made me free.

Verse 2:
[G]I will tell the wondrous [D/F#]story,
[Am]How my [F#dim]lost [G]estate to save,
[F#dim]In His [D/F#]boundless [Am/C]love and [Em]mercy,
[C/G]He the [G]ransom [D7/C]freely [Am]gave.

Verse 3:
[G]I will sing of my [F#dim]Redeemer,
[Am]And His [F#dim]heavenly [G]love to me;
[F#dim]He from [D/F#]death [Bm]to [Am/C]life hath [Em]brought [G]me,
[C/G]Son of [G]God with [D7/C]Him to [Am]be.
